.TH PROCTOR 1 "October 2026" "proctor 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
proctor \- back up, restore and migrate a Prosody XMPP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proctor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proctor
takes consistent, verified backups of a Prosody XMPP installation and restores
or migrates them onto another Linux distribution or BSD system.
It parses the real Prosody configuration instead of assuming a distribution
layout, detects the service manager, backs up filesystem data and
SQLite/PostgreSQL/MySQL storage, preserves ownership and certificates, and
rewrites absolute paths when moving to a host with a different layout.
.PP
Backups are tar archives (gzip, xz, zstd or uncompressed) with a JSON manifest,
per-member SHA-256 checksums and an optional age or GnuPG encryption layer.
A repository stores archives, sidecar manifests, checksums, an index and an
audit log.
.SH OPTIONS
The following options may appear before or after the command.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Use this Proctor JSON configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-repo " " \fIDIR\fR
Use this backup repository directory.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write machine-readable JSON to standard output. Progress and warnings remain on
standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress progress messages.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase detail. Repeat for debug output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable coloured output. The
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable has the same effect.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes for confirmation prompts. Required for non-interactive destructive
commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create the JSON configuration and a mode-0700 repository. Options:
.BR \-\-path " " \fIFILE\fR,
.BR \-\-repo " " \fIDIR\fR,
.BR \-\-force ,
.BR \-\-print ,
.BR \-\-setup ,
.BR \-\-domain " " \fIDOMAIN\fR,
.BR \-\-webserver " " \fIauto|none|nginx|apache\fR,
.BR \-\-certbot " " \fIauto|yes|no\fR,
.BR \-\-email " " \fIADDRESS\fR,
.BR \-\-firewall " " \fIauto|yes|no\fR,
.BR \-\-prosody\-config " " \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.B discover
Show the detected operating system, init system, Prosody paths, storage backend,
database, user/group, virtual hosts and enabled modules.
.TP
.B doctor
Run health checks: privileges, paths, service manager, database clients,
certificate expiry, encryption tools, repository permissions, free space and
backup freshness. Exits non-zero if a check fails.
.TP
.B setup
Detect and interactively install/configure Prosody, nginx or Apache, certbot,
TLS and the XMPP domains. Existing Prosody config is backed up before being
replaced. Options:
.BR \-\-domain " " \fIDOMAIN\fR,
.BR \-\-admin " " \fIJID\fR,
.BR \-\-webserver " " \fIauto|none|nginx|apache\fR,
.BR \-\-certbot " " \fIauto|yes|no\fR,
.BR \-\-email " " \fIADDRESS\fR,
.BR \-\-firewall " " \fIauto|yes|no\fR,
.BR \-\-storage " " \fIinternal_hashed|sqlite\fR,
.BR \-\-proxy\-http ,
.BR \-\-no\-proxy\-http ,
.BR \-\-no\-start ,
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
.BR \-\-force ,
.BR \-\-prosody\-config " " \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.B backup
Create a backup. By default Prosody is stopped briefly for a consistent
snapshot and restarted even if the backup fails. Use
.B \-\-live
for an online backup. Options:
.BR \-\-live ,
.BR \-\-include\-logs ,
.BR \-\-include\-system ,
.BR \-\-letsencrypt " " \fIauto|always|never\fR,
.BR \-\-compression " " \fIgz|xz|zstd|none\fR,
.BR \-\-encrypt ,
.BR \-\-verify ,
.BR \-\-skip\-database ,
.BR \-\-skip\-unreadable ,
.BR \-\-note " " \fITEXT\fR,
.BR \-\-tag " " \fITAG\fR,
.BR \-\-only " " \fICOMPONENT[,..]\fR,
.BR \-\-exclude " " \fICOMPONENT[,..]\fR,
.BR \-\-exclude\-path " " \fIPATH\fR,
.BR \-\-include\-path " " \fIPATH\fR,
.BR \-\-prosody\-config " " \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.BR list " (" ls ")"
List backups with id, time, source, size, encryption, user count and note.
.TP
.BR info " " \fIID\fR
Show the backup manifest summary.
.TP
.BR verify " " \fIID\fR
Verify the archive checksum, the embedded manifest against the sidecar, and the
type, size and SHA-256 of every member. Use
.B \-\-quick
to check only the outer checksum.
.TP
.BR users " " \fIID\fR
List XMPP accounts in a backup. Options:
.BR \-\-domain " " \fIDOMAIN\fR,
.BR \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR,
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.BR restore " " \fIID\fR
Restore onto this host. The archive is verified before any change. By default a
safety backup of the target is created and Prosody is stopped. Options:
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
.BR \-\-only " " \fICOMPONENTS\fR,
.BR \-\-exclude " " \fICOMPONENTS\fR,
.BR \-\-keep\-config ,
.BR \-\-skip\-database ,
.BR \-\-no\-verify ,
.BR \-\-no\-safety\-backup ,
.BR \-\-start ,
.BR \-\-no\-start ,
.BR \-\-map " " \fIOLD=NEW\fR,
.BR \-\-no\-rewrite\-config ,
.BR \-\-no\-overwrite ,
.BR \-\-force ,
.BR \-\-prosody\-config " " \fIFILE\fR,
.BR \-\-install\-missing ,
.BR \-\-no\-install\-missing ,
.BR \-\-webserver " " \fIauto|none|nginx|apache\fR,
.BR \-\-certbot " " \fIauto|yes|no\fR,
.BR \-\-email " " \fIADDRESS\fR,
.BR \-\-firewall " " \fIauto|yes|no\fR,
.BR \-\-admin " " \fIJID\fR,
.BR \-\-proxy\-http ,
.BR \-\-no\-proxy\-http .
.TP
.BR migrate " " \fIID\fR
Same engine as
.BR restore ,
with a migration report and post-move checklist. Intended for a new host.
.TP
.BR export " " \fIID\fR " " \fB\-o\fR " " \fIFILE\fR
Write a portable bundle containing the archive, manifest and checksum.
.B \-\-force
overwrites an existing output file.
.TP
.BR import " " \fIFILE\fR
Import a bundle or raw archive into the repository. Options:
.BR \-\-manifest " " \fIFILE\fR,
.BR \-\-verify .
.TP
.BR diff " " \fIID\fR
Compare a backup's paths, storage, version and user count with this host.
.TP
.B prune
Apply grandfather-father-son retention. It is a dry run unless
.B \-\-apply
is given. Options:
.BR \-\-keep\-last " " \fIN\fR,
.BR \-\-keep\-daily " " \fIN\fR,
.BR \-\-keep\-weekly " " \fIN\fR,
.BR \-\-keep\-monthly " " \fIN\fR.
.TP
.BR delete " " \fIID\fR
Delete one backup.
.B \-\-dry\-run
shows what would be removed.
.TP
.B schedule
Install, remove or show a daily backup schedule. Options:
.BR \-\-install ,
.BR \-\-remove ,
.BR \-\-show ,
.BR \-\-at " " \fIHH:MM\fR,
.BR \-\-type " " \fIauto|systemd|cron\fR,
.BR \-\-cron\-file " " \fIFILE\fR,
.BR \-\-live ,
.BR \-\-command " " \fICOMMAND\fR.
.TP
.BR history
Show the repository audit log.
.B \-\-limit
controls the number of records.
.TP
.B config
Show the effective configuration with password-like fields redacted.
.TP
.B version
Show the Proctor version and Python version.
.SH PROVISIONING
When Prosody is missing on a restore or migration target, Proctor can install
the native Prosody package and, if the backup recorded one, the nginx or Apache
web server plus certbot. It asks before installing unless
.B \-\-install\-missing
is given. Interactive
.B setup
asks for the XMPP domains, admin JID, web server, proxy paths, Let's Encrypt
email and storage backend, then writes a generated Prosody configuration and an
XMPP reverse-proxy vhost. Certbot uses the HTTP-01 webroot flow. If UFW or
firewalld is active, the interactive run offers to open the XMPP and HTTP/HTTPS
ports; non-interactive runs require
.BR \-\-firewall " " \fIyes\fR.
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-install\-missing ,
non-interactive restores only restore files and report missing packages.
.SH COMPONENTS
The values accepted by
.B \-\-only
and
.B \-\-exclude
are:
.BR config ,
.BR certs ,
.BR data ,
.BR plugins ,
.BR letsencrypt ,
.BR logs ,
.BR system ,
.BR extra ,
.BR database .
.PP
By default logs are excluded. Certificates inside the config directory are part
of
.BR config ;
certificate directories elsewhere are
.BR certs ;
referenced Let's Encrypt trees are
.BR letsencrypt .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/proctor/config.json
System configuration when running as root.
.TP
.I ~/.config/proctor/config.json
Per-user configuration.
.TP
.I /var/backups/proctor
Default repository for root.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/proctor/backups
Default repository for a non-root user.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/proctor-backup.service
and
.I /etc/systemd/system/proctor-backup.timer
Installed by
.BR "proctor schedule \-\-install" .
.TP
.I /etc/cron.d/proctor
Cron fallback on systems with a cron.d directory.
.TP
.I /etc/nginx/conf.d/proctor-xmpp.conf
or
.I /etc/nginx/sites-available/proctor-xmpp.conf
Generated nginx reverse proxy.
.TP
.I /etc/apache2/sites-available/proctor-xmpp.conf
or
.I /etc/httpd/conf.d/proctor-xmpp.conf
Generated Apache reverse proxy.
.TP
.I /etc/letsencrypt
Certbot account, renewal and live certificate trees.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General failure, including failed health checks and post-backup restart.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error (including confirmation missing).
.TP
.B 3
Environment or detection error.
.TP
.B 4
Integrity or verification failure.
.TP
.B 5
External command failure (database client, encryption tool, service manager).
.TP
.B 6
Permission denied.
.TP
.B 7
Aborted by the user or interrupt.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create and verify a consistent backup:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo proctor backup \-\-verify
.RE
.fi
.PP
Online backup with encryption:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo proctor backup \-\-live \-\-encrypt \-\-tag protected
.RE
.fi
.PP
Migrate to a host with FreeBSD paths:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo proctor import site.proctorbundle \-\-verify
sudo proctor migrate latest \-\-dry\-run \-\-install\-missing
sudo proctor migrate latest \-\-yes \-\-install\-missing \\
  \-\-map /etc/prosody=/usr/local/etc/prosody \\
  \-\-map /var/lib/prosody=/var/db/prosody
.RE
.fi
.PP
Restore only user data and database, keeping the target config:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo proctor restore latest \-\-yes \-\-keep\-config \-\-only data,database
.RE
.fi
.PP
Guided install of Prosody, nginx and certbot:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo proctor setup \-\-domain example.com \\
  \-\-webserver nginx \-\-certbot yes \-\-email admin@example.com
.RE
.fi
.PP
Daily schedule at 03:30:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo proctor schedule \-\-install \-\-at 03:30
.RE
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Backups contain private keys, password hashes, database credentials and user
data. Store the repository on a protected filesystem and encrypt off-site copies
with
.B \-\-encrypt
(age or GnuPG).
.PP
Restores verify the archive first, reject paths that escape the target, reject
device nodes, refuse to write through symlinked parents unless
.B \-\-force
is given, and write files atomically. Proctor is a root administration tool and
does not protect against an administrator deliberately restoring a malicious
bundle.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Changing the XMPP domain (JIDs) is not supported. POSIX ACLs and extended
attributes are not preserved. Database engine conversion is delegated to
Prosody's own migration tooling. PostgreSQL and MySQL roles/databases must
already exist on the target.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prosody (1),
.BR prosodyctl (1),
.BR age (1),
.BR gpg (1),
.BR tar (1)
.PP
Documentation in
.I docs/
and the project README.
